Here is the commit message:
JS: remove the horizontal scroll bar reset in getInstance for
 ObjectSelector

Fixes a bug introduced way back in 9e89fc6c1fc522327b0bea270a024f51ff5b120c
(JS: Reset ObjectSelector horz scroll bar to 0 on window open)
that caused the horizontal scroll bar to jitter while a model is running.

Signed-off-by: Harry King <d.harry.king@gmail.com>

Here is the root cause:
The bug was caused by the horizontal scroll bar being reset to 0 every time an instance of `ObjectSelector` was created in the `getInstance` method. This frequent resetting led to a jittering effect while a model was running, as the scroll bar would constantly jump back to the start position, disrupting the user's interaction with the UI.

