The code statements that lead to the bug are:
```java
public static synchronized ObjectSelector getInstance() {
    if (myInstance == null)
        myInstance = new ObjectSelector();

    myInstance.treeView.getHorizontalScrollBar().getModel().setValue(0);
}
```
Reason:
The horizontal scroll bar is reset to 0 every time a new instance of `ObjectSelector` is created in the `getInstance` method. This frequent resetting causes the scroll bar to jump back to the start position, leading to a jittering effect while a model is running, disrupting user interaction.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```java
@Override
public void setVisible(boolean bool) {
    if (bool && !isVisible()) {
        myInstance.treeView.getHorizontalScrollBar().getModel().setValue(0);
        myInstance.treeView.getVerticalScrollBar().getModel().setValue(0);
    }
    super.setVisible(bool);
}
```
Reason:
The patch moves the reset of the horizontal scroll bar to the `setVisible` method, which only resets the scroll bar when the `ObjectSelector` is made visible. This prevents the scroll bar from being reset every time an instance is created, thus eliminating the jittering effect while a model is running.

